# Terraform AWS VPC + Docker + GitHub Actions CI/CD

## About

This project demonstrates a complete CI/CD workflow using GitHub Actions, Docker, and Amazon ECR.

The goal of this project was to automate the container image delivery process instead of manually building and pushing Docker images.

Whenever code is pushed to the GitHub repository:

- GitHub Actions automatically starts
- The Docker image is built
- GitHub authenticates securely with AWS using OIDC
- The image is pushed automatically to Amazon ECR

This project builds on the previous projects where Docker images were built and pushed manually.

---

# Technologies Used

- AWS ECR
- GitHub Actions
- Docker
- IAM Roles
- OIDC Authentication
- Linux / WSL Ubuntu
- GitHub
- Nginx

---

# Project Structure

```bash
.
├── .github
│   └── workflows
│       └── build-and-push.yml
│
├── github-actions-ecr-cicd
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   └── app
│       └── index.html
```

---

# How the Pipeline Works

```text
Code Push
   ↓
GitHub Actions Triggered
   ↓
Docker Image Built
   ↓
Authenticate to AWS using OIDC
   ↓
Push Image to Amazon ECR
```

---

# Workflow Explanation

## 1. GitHub Actions Workflow

The workflow file is stored in:

```text
.github/workflows/build-and-push.yml
```

This is required because GitHub only detects workflows from this location.

The workflow automatically runs on every push to the `main` branch.

---

## 2. Docker Build

GitHub Actions builds the Docker image automatically using the Dockerfile inside:

```text
github-actions-ecr-cicd/
```

The Docker image contains a simple Nginx website.

---

## 3. AWS Authentication

Instead of storing AWS credentials inside GitHub Secrets, this project uses:

- IAM Role
- OIDC Authentication

This allows GitHub Actions to securely authenticate to AWS temporarily without permanent credentials.

---

## 4. Push to Amazon ECR

After the image is built:

- GitHub logs into Amazon ECR
- Tags the Docker image
- Pushes the image automatically

The image is then stored in:

```text
Amazon ECR Repository
```

